# Patch:        030-extraction-roots
# Phase:        pre
# Target:       sumcheck/src/hax_roots.rs, sumcheck/src/lib.rs
# Hunks:        2
# Class:        bound
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 4 (aeneas drops a method that no free
#               function calls). `Basis::reduce_claim` is a method, and
#               `lagrange_weights_01inf` is crate-private.
# Cost:         none in a normal build: the module exists only under
#               cfg(hax_backend_lean). In the extracted variant it adds free
#               functions, each of which calls one item of the crate.
#               No existing body changes.
# Upstreamable: no: the module exists only for the extractor.
# Drop when:    charon orders `--start-from` methods, so that the methods
#               themselves can be roots.
# Test:         lint p3-sumcheck unexpected_cfgs
# Mutation:     the module is gated on a misspelled cfg, so a normal
#               `cargo check` reports `unexpected_cfgs`.
#
# The roots are the round arithmetic of the quadratic sumcheck verifier:
#
# - the weights of interpolation through 0, 1 and infinity, and their tensor product;
# - the extrapolation of a quadratic from its values there;
# - the claim reduction of both bases.
#
# The field stays generic, so the Lean model quantifies over every implementation.
#
# The round loop itself is not rooted, for two reasons.
#
# - Its bound `EF: ExtensionField<F>` reaches `PackedFieldExtension::packed_ext_powers`, whose signature aeneas rejects.
# - Its transcript holds a mutable borrow of the challenger, and aeneas finds no fixed point for the loop.
#
